    "dynamic_instructions": "{\r\n  \"datasetView\": \"**Find the Problem**\\n\\nGoal: Find what in the data made Tree 1 get records wrong.\\n\\n1. In **Predict**, choose your label from **My Data** in your guide. In **Using**, choose the two features from **Tree 1** in your guide. Click **Train model**.\\n2. Go to the **Testing** tab. Do steps a and b there.\\n3. Come back to this tab. Do steps c and d:\\n    - c. Click each feature to open Column Analysis. Find the feature whose Least Common category has very few records. Write the feature, its Least Common category and how many records it has in **Find the Problem** in your guide.\\n    - d. Click **Filter**. Choose that category. Write how many records have each label.\\n\\nYou are done when Find the Problem in your guide is full.\",\r\n  \"results\": \"**Find the Problem**\\n\\nGoal: Find what in the data made Tree 1 get records wrong.\\n\\n- a. Click **Accuracy**. Then click **Incorrect**. Write the number incorrect and the number of test records in **Find the Problem** in your guide.\\n- b. Click **Expand columns**. Use **Filter** on one feature at a time. Write the category that most incorrect records share. If none stand out, skip to c.\\n\\nThen go back to the **Dataset** tab for steps c and d.\"\r\n}",
